{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790977491,"nonce":"zr9/bo69qkLdJCHIkcaSA9veK5o=","message":"Refined 2026-10-02: a created issue is described, not diffed.\n\nAn issue absent at the start of the window has no before, so every field read\n`(none) → value`, one line each — the whole issue written the long way. The\nblock line now carries only the marks (`created`, `created, closed`) and one\nindented line follows it:\n\n    - 0ff9c41 Grouped views keep the current group header on the top line — created, closed\n      with status done, priority high, area [tui]\n\nThe fields are the ones it holds at the window's end, in the schema's order for\nits type (`work.schema.export()` keeps that order), skipping `title`, `type`\nand empty values — null, \"\", [], and false, because the one bool a report meets\nis `archived` and a false `archived` is the ordinary case. A field the schema\ndoes not list is appended, sorted, so nothing is dropped silently. A relation is\nstill drawn as the issue it names.\n\nAn issue that existed at the start keeps the `before → after` lines and the\nstatus path unchanged, and comments in the window still follow either kind.\nA created issue's description needed no special case: it is the body of the\ncreate operation, a distinct op type, and never an `add-comment`, so it has\nnever been among the comments listed.\n\nDesign: `doc/design/report.md`, \"The report flow\".","files":null}]}